# WHAT IT COVERS: the 2026-11-02 stream, 44.1 minutes cut to the stretch its video shows, captured
# through Windows.Graphics.Capture with o:vsync on the build that moved the timer modes onto the
# D3D11 present (6017063), the vblank modes' first stream on it. The game hitched (20 to 100 ms)
# 146 times (199 an hour) and stalled for 100 ms or more 48 times (65 an hour), in 42 bursts, 27
# of them with a stall, with no periodic stretch; the dice game runs from about 3.5 minutes into
# the video. The lock released twice, at 2529.25 s, after two hitches of up to 28 ms, and at
# 2567.93 s, 50 ms after the last of five moves in 3.8 s around a 29 ms hitch. The worst blend run, 18
# presents, sits at 1553.1 s at the end of a burst of 7 hitches and 3 stalls of up to 424 ms. Of
# the 20 moves on the replay, 2 of them late, 3 land more than 2 ms from a real frame.
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 56.073 s, from the 2073
# marked frames in its first 34 s, all on time within 0.38 ms of that offset (p90). The video
# runs 2647.6 s with no holes. It opens on gameplay (marked), shows about 20 s of the journal and
# map at about 50 s, and ends on gameplay; the cut is the whole video, 56.1 s to 2703.7 s. Before
# it, the lock settled with 15 releases in the log's first 43 s. Inside the cut, 11 seconds in 11
# runs fall out of the 60 fps regime, each a single hitch second.
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships, so the two lines are comparable. The
# replay line reads synth 0.5% against 0.5%, worst run 18 against 18, runs >= 50 0 against 0 and
# pull wraps 33 against 32. On the dejitter arm, which is how the stream ran, blends are 766
# against 770, repeats 504 against 503, skips 106 against 106, pull wraps 43.6 an hour against
# 43.5 and the worst run 18 against 18. The replay makes 20 moves, 2 late, and the field's log
# has 20, 2 late, in the window; both field releases match the replay's within 0.34 ms, with none
# on one side only. The planner line reads 771 of 771 synthesized presents planned by the step
# against 738 by a guessed target; in the field the window's 770 synthesized presents were all
# planned (721 warped from a flow handed over earlier, 49 drawn as the blend because the flow was
# handed over at that present, none unplanned).
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran. The worst run is 18 on both arms.
